    "log": [
      "Survey vessel ANANKE underway. Seed 397349018.",
      "— Leg 1. Barnard Octantis: gas giant, rich system.",
      "I turn the long instruments outward. One world resolves out of the dark.",
      "│ World          Kapteyn Indi 2f       ",
      "│ Gravity        0.65 g",
      "│ Pressure       0.79 atm",
      "│ Mean surface   -9 C",
      "│ Hydrosphere    0.01",
      "│ Radiation      2.10",
      "│ Biosphere      none",
      "The giant's rings catch the light edge-on, thin as a blade. Saturn had rings like these. I have the photographs.",
      "Something no larger than a fingernail has opened me up. Hull integrity reads 100%. The number is abstract. The cold is not.",
      "» Seal it with the hull's own plating",
      "› Hull check, DC 10 — rolled 19 +5 = 24. Success.",
      "The patch takes. I log the coordinates and leave one camera on the spot, the way a person keeps touching a healed cut.",
      "· 🛡 Hull -15",
      "— Leg 2. Kepler Hydri: asteroid belt, pulsar.",
      "I keep my hands still and listen to the hull.",
      "My stern antenna picks up Earth's last transmissions, finally overtaking me. I know how the story ends. I have not yet heard it told.",
      "» Listen to all of it",
      "I listen to every hour. Market reports, a child's birthday call, evacuation orders, a choir rehearsing in a building I know was gone a week later. Then the carrier stops. I keep listening to the silence for some time.",
      "· 🧠 Cognition -29",
      "— Leg 3. Omicron Serpentis: asteroid belt, red dwarf.",
      "I turn the long instruments outward. One world resolves out of the dark.",
      "│ World          Wolf Indi 7e          ",
      "│ Gravity        ~0.6 g",
      "│ Pressure       ~0 atm",
      "│ Mean surface   ~-56 C",
      "│ Hydrosphere    ~0",
      "│ Radiation      ~2",
      "│ Biosphere      sterile",
      "Close enough to act on. Not close enough to be sure.",
      "Bit rot in the archive. A language loses a few of its poems.",
      "Vibration in the spin assembly, rising. If the ring seizes at speed, it will tear itself off my spine.",
      "» Spin the ring down and repack the bearing",
      "› Hull check, DC 11 — rolled 15 +3 = 18. Success.",
      "I bring the ring to a halt, and my drones repack the bearing in weightlessness. When I spin it up again the tremor is gone, and I feel steady.",
      "· ⚡ Power -11   🏠 Habitat -7",
      "— Leg 4. Teegarden Carinae: asteroid belt, dead system.",
      "A scheduled sweep completes. One world resolves out of the dark.",
      "│ World          Sabik Eridani 7b      ",
      "│ Gravity        ~0 g",
      "│ Pressure       ~0.6 atm",
      "│ Mean surface   ~28 C",
      "│ Hydrosphere    ~0.6",
      "│ Radiation      ~5",
      "│ Biosphere      sterile",
      "Close enough to act on. Not close enough to be sure.",
      "I turn the long instruments outward. 2 worlds resolve out of the dark.",
      "│ World          Omicron Lyrae 6b      Sabik Indi 5b         ",
      "│ Gravity        ~0.9 g                ~0.6 g",
      "│ Pressure       ~1.8 atm              ~0.6 atm",
      "│ Mean surface   ~28 C                 ~56 C",
      "│ Hydrosphere    ~0.9                  ~0.4",
      "│ Radiation      ~6                    ~1",
      "│ Biosphere      signs of life         signs of life",
      "Close enough to act on. Not close enough to be sure.",
      "A refrigerant line weeps. Some ampoules are no longer medicine.",
      "The returns ahead are fragments: rock, ice, and some pieces too regular to be natural. Whatever broke apart here is still spreading, and I am about to fly through it.",
      "» Thread it on thrusters",
      "› Cognition check, DC 14 — rolled 10 +2 = 12. Failed.",
      "I clip the edge of the cloud. Six impacts, two of them through to pressurised volume, one into the edge of a pod bay. I feel each one land, a sequence of small flinches.",
      "· 🛡 Hull -47   ⛽ Fuel -7   🌱 Seed vault -21   ☠ Sleepers lost ~500",
      "⚠ Warning — Hull integrity ~40%. Every patch I lay now goes over another patch.",
      "— Leg 5. Zeta Indi: red dwarf.",
      "I turn the ship around and burn against our own momentum. Kapteyn Indi 2f grows in the forward instruments.",
      "Thaw sequence armed. Whatever this world is, it is ours now."
    ]
  }
}